What is the worst-case time complexity of this binary search on a sorted list of length n?

```python
def has(arr, t):
    if not arr:
        return False
    mid = len(arr) // 2
    if arr[mid] == t:
        return True
    # Each slice creates a new list.
    if arr[mid] < t:
        return has(arr[mid+1:], t)
    return has(arr[:mid], t)
```

